# Fictional EP Tracklist

## Track 1: Down-Bow Lands Where the Low Tom Was

**Story & Context:** The debut runs at 134 BPM. Caio begins with a stripped tamborzão pattern containing one conspicuously missing low-tom hit in the second half of the bar. Elin fills that exact vacancy with a heavy down-bow open fifth on the nyckelharpa. The bowed attack is not bass-heavy enough to mimic the drum, but its friction and body resonance make the absence feel intentional.

On the next cycle, Elin reverses to a lighter up-bow while Caio restores the low tom and removes the clap instead. Marina replaces every fourth programmed low hit with one muted surdo stroke. Oskar answers only the strongest down-bow reversals with a dry prepared-electric-piano fifth. Rafael waits until Elin moves into the upper register, then adds one low bass-clarinet pedal for two bars.

At the midpoint, the Bow Flip Matrix reverses: up-bows now align with low-drum space and down-bows occur against silence. The track feels reweighted without changing harmony or tempo. The final bar contains the original missing low-tom position, but Elin also withholds the down-bow, leaving the gap completely empty.

