## Track 2: Key Seventeen Clicks Before the Surdo Opens

**Story & Context:** The second track runs at 138 BPM and emphasizes the nyckelharpa keybox. Elin plays a repeated three-note cell requiring one especially audible wooden key release. Caio places a short clipped snare immediately after that release, making the keybox sound function like a pickup into the electronic hit.

Marina alternates muted and open surdo strokes every two bars. The open stroke is allowed only after key seventeen has released, creating a clear mechanical-to-acoustic sequence. Oskar plays two prepared electric-piano notes a minor seventh apart after each open surdo. Rafael contributes short dry descending fourths in the spaces where the nyckelharpa stops.

During the last minute, Caio removes all upper electronic percussion. Key clicks, bow changes, and surdo become the entire top-and-mid rhythmic field above the kick and short analog sub. The track ends with one wooden key release after the drums have already stopped.

