## Track 3: Sympathetic Strings Keep the Floor Moving

**Story & Context:** The closer begins at 130 BPM with the sparsest arrangement on the EP. Elin holds a two-note drone while Caio uses only kick, one low tom, and occasional clap. Every fourth bar Elin stops bowing abruptly, exposing the sympathetic strings ringing beneath the silence.

Each exposed halo causes Caio to remove the following low-tom event. Marina answers with a soft hand-damped surdo stroke one beat later, while Oskar remains silent so the resonance stays visible. Rafael adds breath-only bass-clarinet attacks during the first two halos, then introduces actual pitch only in the final third.

In the closing section, Elin shortens the bowed phrase by one beat every cycle, so sympathetic resonance occupies more and more of the bar. The drums become correspondingly sparser until only kick and surdo remain. The final nyckelharpa release rings alone for several seconds with no electronic tail.

